.resources/TASK-260720-12iigs/TASK-260720-12iigs_review-accepted.md:5:Implementation review found no defects. Receipt v1 is a closed four-field schema whose strict shared input requires schema version 1, go-v1, curator-build-source-v1, build root, command, source directory, native GOOS/GOARCH/tuning, curator-go-toolchain-v1, all eleven fixed policy values, and exactly one closed artifact path/hash/size record. Forbidden provenance booleans and physical cache, receipt, and lock paths are rejected. Marker v2 preserves the marker-v1 surface, permits skill schema versions 0 through 6, requires build_roots and builds, requires build_source exactly for non-empty builds, and stores closed per-command driver/cache-key/receipt-hash/artifact-hash/artifact-path records. Protocol prose is the normative lexical-order rule because Draft 2020-12 cannot express generic array or object-key sorting; generated valid-multiple-builds plus Go assertions verify sorted build_roots and build keys. Generated/indexed coverage contains 16 receipt cases and 14 marker cases spanning valid, required, conditional, unknown, version/driver/algorithm/policy/hash/path mismatches.
