I found a concrete fail-open condition despite the green suite: the telemetry config directory can be replaced by an outward symlink during `go telemetry off`. The code then validates `GOTELEMETRYDIR` only against that relocated config path, accepts telemetry outside the operation-private root, deletes the nominal root, and leaves the external telemetry state behind. I reproduced the false acceptance directly and am finishing the remaining regression/scope checks before recording `changes_requested`.
